    "durationMs": 262157,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and verified. Summary of what I built and found:\n\n**Implementation**\n- Rails 8.0 API-only app (`~> 8.0.2`) with a `links` table (`code` unique-indexed + non-null, `url` text, `clicks` integer default 0) via a single migration\n- `LinksController` — create (generates an 8-char code from `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` when omitted, enforces the 4–20 char code format), index (ascending by id with `total`), show\n- `RedirectsController` — `GET /r/{code}` does `Link.increment_counter` (exactly one atomic increment) then `head :found` with the exact stored URL in `Location`; routes use `format: false` so codes like `abc.def` are never split into a format suffix\n- Errors: 409 duplicate code (with a `RecordNotUnique` fallback for races), 404 unknown code, 422 for missing/invalid url, invalid code, non-string params, and malformed JSON (via `rescue_from ActionDispatch::Http::Parameters::ParseError`)\n- `config/database.yml` reads everything from `DATABASE_URL`; nothing hard-coded\n- `start.sh` runs `db:prepare` (applies pending migrations) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup\n\n**One notable issue fixed**: bundler pulled `json` 3.1.0, but Rails 8.0's JSON encoder still passes the removed `quirks_mode` option, which made every JSON render/parse fail with 500s. I pinned `gem \"json\", \"~> 2.9\"` (installed 2.21.2) in the Gemfile.\n\n**Verified end-to-end** (curl against `sh start.sh`, including a restart): 201 creates with generated/custom codes echoing the URL unchanged, 409 duplicates, 404s, 422s for all invalid inputs, 302 redirects with exact Location, click counts incrementing exactly once and surviving restarts, and list ordering. The database was truncated afterward so the test suite starts clean, and my server instance is stopped."
